{"type": "message", "id": "335351da", "parentId": "52480496", "timestamp": "2026-04-24T09:01:29.490Z", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_50ludl2yi4cuu8kh4b46o1od", "toolName": "web_search", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "{\n  \"query\": \"llama3 70b zero-shot relation extraction symmetric noise site:arxiv.org\",\n  \"provider\": \"brave\",\n  \"count\": 5,\n  \"tookMs\": 991,\n  \"externalContent\": {\n    \"untrusted\": true,\n    \"source\": \"web_search\",\n    \"provider\": \"brave\",\n    \"wrapped\": true\n  },\n  \"results\": [\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d45e0912a6e18db\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Uniqueness of LLaMA3-70B Series with Per-Channel Quantization\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"0d45e0912a6e18db\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.15301v2\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a1e8fdcae5ea550a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis approach <strong>significantly reduces the dynamic range required for quantization, enabling the LLaMA3-70B model series to retain accuracy comparable to their FP16 counterparts. In this paper, we use symmetric integer-bit quantization due to its high efficiency and simpler hardware support</strong>.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a1e8fdcae5ea550a\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"October 1, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"377209f4d69e2e30\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nRELATE: Relation Extraction in Biomedical Abstracts with LLMs and Ontology Constraints\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"377209f4d69e2e30\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2509.19057\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85692038132d6e91\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe experimented with MedGemma (4B), LLaMA2 (7B), LLaMA3 (8B), LLaMA3 (70B), MedGemma (27B), and OpenAI GPT-4o-mini (unknown number of parameters). The last two demonstrated greater consistency and fewer hallucinations compared to the other models. Since those two models had very similar ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"85692038132d6e91\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 27, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7963b753ecd7c0ce\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThe Uniqueness of LLaMA3-70B with Per-Channel Quantization: An Empirical Study\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"7963b753ecd7c0ce\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2408.15301v1\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63dce63cd1ca2bef\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nThis approach applies per-group ... This mixed strategy effectively restores the accuracy of the LLaMA3-70B model series to levels comparable to its FP16 counterparts. In this paper, we use symmetric integer-bit quantization due to its high efficiency and simpler hardware ...\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"63dce63cd1ca2bef\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 27, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e709f9b044badf2a\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nA Practice of Post-Training on Llama-3 70B with Optimal Selection of Additional Language Mixture Ratio\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"e709f9b044badf2a\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2409.06624v3\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9b4c2c8fe311698\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe collect online conversation data for one week, and compare it with the responses of Llama3-70B-Instruct and GPT4 upon the same query. To examine the response qualities, pairwise evaluations are conducted by human annotators among three models, with the win rates shown in Table 8.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"a9b4c2c8fe311698\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"August 9, 2025\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"title\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5d885541b7f310f\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nZeFaV: Boosting Large Language Models for Zero-shot Fact Verification\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"b5d885541b7f310f\\\">>>\",\n      \"url\": \"https://arxiv.org/html/2411.11247\",\n      \"description\": \"\\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"184b9dde63c76442\\\">>>\\nSource: Web Search\\n---\\nWe perform ZeFaV on Meta-Llama-3-70B-Instruct222https://huggingface.co/meta-llama/Meta-Llama-3-70B-Instruct and evaluate the performance on the division of HoVer [9] and FEVEROUS-S [2] datasets by Pan et al. [14] through the F1-score metric. We run the LLMs with LoRA technique [8] quantized to 4 bits, and the maximum length for the generation model is 2,048.\\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\\\"184b9dde63c76442\\\">>>\",\n      \"published\": \"November 18, 2024\",\n      \"siteName\": \"arxiv.org\"\n    }\n  ]\n}"}], "details": {"query": "llama3 70b zero-shot relation extraction symmetric noise site:arxiv.org", "provider": "brave", "count": 5, "tookMs": 991, "externalContent": {"untrusted": true, "source": "web_search", "provider": "brave", "wrapped": true}, "results": [{"title": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d45e0912a6e18db\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThe Uniqueness of LLaMA3-70B Series with Per-Channel Quantization\n<<<END_EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"0d45e0912a6e18db\">>>", "url": "https://arxiv.org/html/2408.15301v2", "description": "\n<<<EXTERNAL_UNTRUSTED_CONTENT id=\"a1e8fdcae5ea550a\">>>\nSource: Web Search\n---\nThis approach <strong>significantly reduces the dynamic range required for quantization, enabling the LLaMA3-70B model series to retain accuracy comparable to their FP16 counterparts. In this paper, we use symmetric integer-bit quantization due to its hig